-- title:
--   Characters inherit translation relations of a nonzero continuous function
-- statement:
--   Let $G$ be a commutative group with a topology making it a Hausdorff topological group whose underlying space is compact, written multiplicatively. Let $f : G \to \mathbb{C}$ be a continuous function with $f \neq 0$, and let $R$ be a set of finitely supported functions $r : G \to \mathbb{C}$, thought of as linear relations among translates. Assume that $f$ satisfies every relation in $R$ at every point: for each $r \in R$ and each $x \in G$, the finite sum $\sum_{g \in \operatorname{supp}(r)} r(g)\, f(x g)$ vanishes. The conclusion is that there exists a group homomorphism $\chi : G \to \mathbb{C}^{\times}$ which is continuous (as a map to the units of $\mathbb{C}$ with their topology) and which satisfies the same relations numerically: for every $r \in R$, the finite sum $\sum_{g \in \operatorname{supp}(r)} r(g)\, \chi(g)$, with $\chi(g)$ viewed in $\mathbb{C}$, vanishes. No non-degeneracy is required of the elements of $R$, and $R$ may be empty, finite or infinite.
--
--   This is the form of harmonic analysis on a compact abelian group needed downstream: by Peter–Weyl the closed translation-invariant subspace of $L^2(G)$ generated by $f$ is spanned by the continuous characters it contains, so some character satisfies all the translation relations that $f$ does. It is cited in the Langlands–Tunnell part of the development, in the converse-theorem step [`LanglandsTunnell.Converse.eq_zero_or_exists_agreesAwayFromFinite_eisensteinTableOf_of_unipotent_invariant`](thm.html#LanglandsTunnell.Converse.eq_zero_or_exists_agreesAwayFromFinite_eisensteinTableOf_of_unipotent_invariant) and in [`LanglandsTunnell.CubicInduction.isCuspidalAlong_form_of_tempered_of_entire_eulerTwists`](thm.html#LanglandsTunnell.CubicInduction.isCuspidalAlong_form_of_tempered_of_entire_eulerTwists), the proof proceeding through the compact self-adjoint convolution operators provided by [`MeasureTheory.L2.exists_convolutionCLM_isCompactOperator_of_compactSpace`](thm.html#MeasureTheory.L2.exists_convolutionCLM_isCompactOperator_of_compactSpace).
-- source:
